-- title:
--   Serre–Tate existence of Weierstrass lifts of formal groups
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$, and $E_0$ an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ whose formal group $E_0.\mathrm{formalGroup}$ (the group law `formalGroupLawFixed`, obtained by substituting `fgZ3Fixed` into `fgInv`) satisfies `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`: taken with respect to the ideal $\bot$ of $k$, there is a unit power series $u$ with the $q$-th series `nthSeries q` of that formal group equal to $u$ times its Drinfeld divisor `drinfeldDivisor q 0 0`. Let $W_0$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal, with maximal ideal generated by $q$, and let $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ be a surjective ring homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal. Let $T$ be an Artinian local commutative $W_0$-algebra with a surjective ring homomorphism $\mathrm{res}_T : T \to k$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal of $T$ and which restricts to $\mathrm{res}_0$ along the structure map $W_0 \to T$. Let $G$ be a commutative formal group over $T$ with $G.\mathrm{IsBaseChange}\ \mathrm{res}_T\ E_0.\mathrm{formalGroup}$, i.e. the power series of $E_0.\mathrm{formalGroup}$ is the image of that of $G$ under $\mathrm{res}_T$. Then there exist a Weierstrass curve $E$ over $T$ with $E.\mathrm{map}\ \mathrm{res}_T = E_0$, a formal group $G'$ over $T$ whose power series is $E.\mathrm{formalGroupLawFixed}$, and an isomorphism of formal group laws $\psi : G' \to G$ (a power series with zero constant term and unit linear coefficient intertwining the two laws) whose coefficients satisfy $\mathrm{res}_T(\mathrm{coeff}_n \psi) = 1$ for $n = 1$ and $0$ otherwise, so that $\psi$ reduces to the identity series modulo the maximal ideal of $T$.
--
--   This is the existence half of Serre–Tate theory in Weierstrass coordinates: over an Artinian local base with residue field $k$, every commutative formal-group deformation of the formal group of $E_0$ comes, up to a $\star$-isomorphism reducing to the identity, from a Weierstrass lift of $E_0$. It is used in the construction of rigid data on modular curves, through [`ModularCurve.LevelModuliPackageAbs.exists_raw_lawIso_appAdic_eq_of_isDrinfeldBasisAdic_rigidDataH1Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LevelModuliPackageAbs.exists_raw_lawIso_appAdic_eq_of_isDrinfeldBasisAdic_rigidDataH1Pow).
